Risk free rate: 
The risk free rate is understood as the rate of return on an asset that is theoretically free of any risks. 
Therefore, the weighted average yield of Government of India Securities at the time of decision making 
are considered as risk free rate. This data is published by Reserve Bank of India. (Source: RBI). 

The applicable risk free rate is 7.524%19.
